# Local environment.
#
# .env.production IS committed, deliberately. Everything in it is a VITE_ value,
# which means it is substituted into the JavaScript bundle and served to every
# visitor — it is published the moment the panel deploys, so keeping it out of
# git buys no secrecy and costs the build its configuration. Committing it is
# what lets a clone build correctly with nothing configured at the host.
#
# Nothing without a VITE_ prefix belongs in that file. Vite would not expose it,
# but git would.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
